Subject: Mantle's changes: MD5, fallible digests, a digest's state, one-shot HMAC, TLS 1.3 vectored sealing, AES-CBC-HMAC, AES-192 key wrap, a cloneable LessSafeKey
Why: Mantle (vendored at vendor/mantle, kiln's CP-T10.2) builds on these, which upstream doesn't have: S3's ETags and Content-MD5 are MD5; production code never panics (Context::try_new, try_update, try_finish); a native upload keeps its object's MD5 running across the runs it's cut into (digest::State, Context::state and resume); hmac::sign_once's one-shot HMAC (187 ns where a copied Key took 255 ns); TLS 1.3 records sealed from several slices at once; JWE's A128CBC-HS256 to A256CBC-HS512 and A192KW; LessSafeKey cloned through EVP_AEAD_CTX_copy (aws/aws-lc-rs#1165); and autotests on, so the tests these add run. Mantle made them on 1.18.1 (its vendor/UPSTREAM.md at 17eb8032); here they are on 1.18.2, the release kiln takes, where they apply unchanged.

